    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0819" n="809" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.288M/12–3147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-31T13:00:00-05:00">December 31,
                            1947—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1586. Current situation in Manchuria, as described Changchun’s Tel 260 Dec
                        22<anchor n="2" xml:id="d709-f1"/> presumably rptd Emb, and particularly
                    increasing difficulty and hazardous communications leads Dept seriously to
                    question retention ConGen Changchun. Can this office be closed and personnel
                    withdrawn without fanfare since Dept wishes to avoid adverse effect on ChiGovt’s
                    position Manchuria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
